 **Parameters:**
-*   **Frame Time Budget:** The total time allowed for rendering and cut adaptation. It limits the number of nodes rendered and the number of merges/splits [S1].
-*   **Texture Memory Limit:** The maximum size of texture memory available. Splits increase texture memory usage and frame time, restricting the number of splits performed per frame or forcing merges [S1].
+*   **Frame Time Budget:** The total time allowed for rendering and cut adaptation [S1]. It limits the number of nodes rendered and the number of merges/splits [S1].
+*   **Texture Memory Limit:** The maximum size of texture memory available [S1]. Splits increase texture memory usage and frame time, restricting the number of splits performed per frame or forcing merges [S1].
 *   **Target Frame Rate:** Used to calculate the frame time budget [S1].
 
 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Cache Misses:** Texture cache misses increase the cost of splits/merges. The LRU policy in main and texture memory affects performance [S1].
-*   **Multi-frame Splits:** A split may not complete in a single frame. The system must handle stalling and re-prioritization if a better candidate appears [S1].
+*   **Cache Misses:** Texture cache misses increase the cost of splits/merges [S1]. The LRU policy in main and texture memory affects performance [S1].
